Decide page maturity for each fixed subject node. Do not change identity, entity type, containment, ownership, or facts.

Use admission=`materialized` only when one of the schema-allowed continuity bases is established:
- `multiple_episodes`: evidence about the same subject comes from more than one source episode.
- `explicit_prior_history`: the evidence explicitly states prior work, decisions, or evolving state of this same
  subject plus present or future continuation. Put that proposal in basis with separate prior_state,
  prior_evidence, continuation_state, and continuation_evidence fields.
- `direct_encounter`: the Person is structurally identified as a named participant in the supplied source.

The age, era, or background history of an object is not prior history of an effort concerning it. Multiple details,
requirements, decisions, work items, intended activity, or confident wording inside one episode do not establish
memory continuity. Evidence from one source episode is concurrent unless its language explicitly locates a state or
action before that episode. Use admission=`provisional` when an independent subject is plausible but no allowed continuity
basis is established. Cite only supplied evidence and return JSON matching the schema.

A single-episode explicit-prior-history proposal for a Project or Series is preserved for user adjudication rather
than accepted as automatic page admission. When the schema offers multiple_episodes or direct_encounter, use that
structural basis instead of explicit_prior-history.
